WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:05.540
Welcome to the ultimate go-to guide for choosing
an iPad in 2019.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:11.820
Now that the new iPad Air and iPad Mini are
available, Apple’s 2019 iPad lineup is complete,

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:17.590
alongside the 2018 budget iPad and 2018 iPad
Pro. and I personally think this is it until

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:18.590
next year.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:22.490
There’s no reason for Apple to update the
budget iPad until next year, since they’ll

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:27.250
have to raise the price into the iPad Mini’s
territory, and same for the iPad Pro, since

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.710
the hardware is already way ahead of the current
iOS software.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:34.260
So with four iPads in the lineup, how in the
world do you choose one?

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.160
Well, I’m confident that by the end of this
video, you’ll be able to make up your mind!

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.750
And we’re gonna have links to the best sales
on each of these iPads in the description

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.110
below so check those out if you make up your
mind!

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.110
Let’s get started with design differences.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:48.750
All three non-pro iPads look basically identical
on the back side.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:53.080
The Pro looks much different with a darker
space gray finish, antenna bar at the top,

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:58.180
and a large camera bump, which none of the
other iPads get, but it’s for good reason,

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:00.010
as you’ll see in the camera comparison.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:04.610
The Pro also gets the smart connector on the
back since it uses magnets to attach to the

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:09.880
smart keyboard, and the iPad Air is also the
only non-Pro iPad ever to get the smart connector,

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:10.880
but it’s on the side.

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:14.920
The iPad Pro is also the only iPad out of
this lineup that gets four speakers, two on

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:19.500
the bottom and two on top, and as you’ll
hear later, it destroys the others in the

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.640
sound comparison.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.220
Another difference is USB-C on the Pro, but
you can’t really do much with it yet.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:29.990
But you do get a faster 18W charger compared
to the old 12W charger that comes with the

00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:30.990
rest of these iPads.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:36.020
Of course, the Pro gets the new modern square-edged
design that also comes with rounded corners

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:40.070
on the display, making the other iPads look
outdated compared to it.

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:44.630
However, the Pro is the only iPad that doesn’t
get a headphone jack, which sucks for a lot

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:48.960
of people, but it makes for the thinnest iPad
out of the lineup, which is nice, but it led

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:52.840
to some bendgate issues, which I personally
haven’t experienced at all.

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:57.600
The Pro has even bezels all-around thanks
to the removal of Touch ID and the switch

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.720
to Face ID, which by the way, works great
since there’s no notch and you can use it

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.510
in any orientation, even upside down.

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:07.840
Some people still prefer Touch ID though,
and that’s totally fine.

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:13.989
The Pro has smaller bezels than the 2018 iPad,
but both the 2019 Air and Mini actually have

00:02:13.989 --> 00:02:15.659
slimmer bezels on the side.

00:02:15.659 --> 00:02:20.819
Moving onto display differences, the new Air
and Mini have literally identical displays,

00:02:20.819 --> 00:02:26.049
but the Mini packs the same amount of pixels
into the smaller 7.9” display, so it has

00:02:26.049 --> 00:02:29.840
the highest pixels per inch out of the whole
iPad lineup, including the Pro, and it also

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.819
comfortably fits in one hand so it’s the
lightest and most portable out of all of these.

00:02:33.819 --> 00:02:38.779
The 2018 budget iPad is the only one that
doesn’t get a fully laminated display, which

00:02:38.779 --> 00:02:41.879
basically means the display is glued to the
glass.

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:46.450
This leads to it looking a little grey, lacking
deep blacks like the rest, and there’s a

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:51.090
gap between the display and the glass which
is noticeable from an angle, and especially

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.499
while using the Apple Pencil.

00:02:52.499 --> 00:02:56.660
It’s also the only one that doesn’t have
an anti-reflective coating, so you’ll notice

00:02:56.660 --> 00:02:58.370
reflections a lot more.

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:03.109
It doesn’t get P3 wide-color gamut either,
like the other iPads, which makes for a very

00:03:03.109 --> 00:03:05.939
color accurate display with colors that really
pop.

00:03:05.939 --> 00:03:10.629
It also lacks True Tone, which automatically
adjusts the display’s color balance to match

00:03:10.629 --> 00:03:12.260
the environment you’re in.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.129
I personally love True Tone!

00:03:14.129 --> 00:03:19.280
So as you can see, the 2018 budget iPad is
really lacking in the display department.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.299
Now the 2018 iPad Pro gets a couple more things,
it boasts 600 nits of brightness compared

00:03:24.299 --> 00:03:29.549
to 500 on the 2019 iPads and around 450 on
the budget iPad.

00:03:29.549 --> 00:03:33.110
The iPad Pro also gets ProMotion, which is
huge in my book!

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:37.939
It allows the display to refresh at up to
120Hz and dynamically go down to match the

00:03:37.939 --> 00:03:41.499
frame rate of the content you’re viewing
to save battery life.

00:03:41.499 --> 00:03:45.669
As you can see in this slow-mo clip, the difference
in the smoothness of ProMotion compared to

00:03:45.669 --> 00:03:48.569
the other iPads in this lineup is huge!

00:03:48.569 --> 00:03:51.239
And trust me, you’ll feel this difference
every day!

00:03:51.239 --> 00:03:56.360
Not only that, but ProMotion lowers the latency
of the Apple Pencil as well, and you can easily

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:00.139
see the difference compared to the other iPads
in this slow-mo clip.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:04.459
Speaking of the Apple Pencil, all of the iPads
support it, but the Pro supports the new Apple

00:04:04.459 --> 00:04:07.120
Pencil 2, which is better in every way.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.750
You don’t have to plug it into the side
like on the other iPads.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:14.349
It magnetically attaches to the side and instantly
starts pairing and charging.

00:04:14.349 --> 00:04:18.120
The new matte finish feels a lot better in
the hand and it comes with a new double-tap

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:21.319
to switch tools feature which is incredibly
convenient.

00:04:21.319 --> 00:05:06.099
Now let’s get into that speaker comparison,
and make sure to put on some headphones.

00:05:06.099 --> 00:05:09.680
Before we get into performance and gaming,
let’s quickly compare the cameras.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:14.419
The Pro gets flash on the rear with a 12MP
sensor compared to 8 on the other iPads, and

00:05:14.419 --> 00:05:18.900
here’s a photo comparison between them,
the Pro obviously looks better than the others.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:23.629
The Pro is also the only one that can shoot
4K video at 60 frames per second.

00:05:23.629 --> 00:05:29.409
On the front-side, the budget iPad only gets
a 1.2MP sensor compared to 7MP on the other

00:05:29.409 --> 00:05:33.970
iPads, so selfies look horrible compared to
the other iPads, especially the Pro since

00:05:33.970 --> 00:05:37.060
it gets Portrait mode thanks to the Face ID
sensors.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:41.560
The Pro also gets 5 microphones instead of
2 on the other iPads so it sounds much better

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.070
as well.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:52.930
Now let’s finally get into performance!

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:59.249
The budget iPad only gets 2GB of RAM compared
to 3 on the 2019 iPads and 4 on the Pro.

00:05:59.249 --> 00:06:03.819
But you can also get up to 6GB on the Pro
if you buy the 1TB model, but it’s not worth

00:06:03.819 --> 00:06:05.539
the cash for almost everyone.

00:06:05.539 --> 00:06:11.120
The budget iPad gets the A10 processor, compared
to the A12 on the 2019 iPads and the A12X

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.680
on the Pro.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:17.020
The budget iPads A10 is also the only one
that doesn’t come with the neural engine.

00:06:17.020 --> 00:06:21.199
Getting into the Geekbench 4 benchmark, the
budget iPad is way behind the others in terms

00:06:21.199 --> 00:06:26.960
of single-core, and even more behind in multi-core,
with the Air and Mini almost doubling the

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:29.629
score, and the Pro almost tripling the score!

00:06:29.629 --> 00:06:35.009
In the Metal test, the Air and Mini are around
75% faster than the budget iPad, and the iPad

00:06:35.009 --> 00:06:41.129
Pro is almost 2x faster than the 2019 iPads,
and over 3x faster than the budget iPad.

00:06:41.129 --> 00:06:45.389
In Antutu’s 3D benchmark, there isn’t
as big of a difference now, but the iPad Pro

00:06:45.389 --> 00:06:49.159
is still around 2.5x faster than the 2018
iPad.

00:06:49.159 --> 00:06:55.600
Finally, for a more realistic test, we exported
a 1-minute 4K 60p video on each of the iPads,

00:06:55.600 --> 00:07:00.780
and the iPad Pro finished 4x sooner than the
budget iPad, and it was over twice as fast

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:02.590
as the 2019 iPads.

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:05.550
This is where you’ll actually feel the power
of the new iPad Pro.

00:07:05.550 --> 00:07:07.610
And now let’s talk about gaming.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:12.110
Each of these iPads apart from the budget
iPad can run Fortnite at High graphics at

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:13.550
60 frames per second.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:17.080
The budget iPad can only run Medium graphics
at 30 frames per second.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:22.349
And that’s the same story for other games
like Asphalt 9, running at 30 instead of 60

00:07:22.349 --> 00:07:24.009
like on the other iPads.

00:07:24.009 --> 00:07:27.870
The graphics are noticeably worse and I also
noticed some dropped frames while gaming.

00:07:27.870 --> 00:07:34.950
The iPad Air, Mini and Pro all run Fortnite
and Asphalt 9 perfectly at 60 fps, no dropped

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:39.659
frames or issues at all, so the extra power
of the Pro isn’t really being used for almost

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:40.939
every game on the app store.

00:07:40.939 --> 00:07:45.150
Out of all of them, the iPad Mini is by far
the most comfortable to hold in the hand while

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:46.150
gaming.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:48.930
The others weigh quite a bit more so your
hands will get tired over time.

00:07:48.930 --> 00:07:53.169
Let’s quickly mention some other spec differences
before I start recommending which iPad you

00:07:53.169 --> 00:07:54.169
should buy.

00:07:54.169 --> 00:07:59.750
The budget iPad gets Bluetooth 4.2 compared
to 5.0 on the other iPads, which also get

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:04.210
simultaneous dual-band WiFi for more bandwidth
and a more reliable connection.

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:07.509
They also get Gigabit-class LTE if you’re
buying that model.

00:08:07.509 --> 00:08:10.360
Now with all of that said, which iPad should
you buy?

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:15.499
Well, the iPad Pro is obviously the best and
most powerful iPad, but it’s also the most

00:08:15.499 --> 00:08:17.689
expensive, at $800.

00:08:17.689 --> 00:08:21.840
The four speakers and ProMotion technology
make a huge difference in daily use, but if

00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:26.129
you’re not gonna be doing high-end editing
or anything that can use the power of the

00:08:26.129 --> 00:08:30.570
A12X chip, you’ll probably be better off
with the 2019 iPad Air.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:34.740
If you’ve got extra cash, you love the new
design and you want to keep it for over 5

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:39.349
years, the Pro may be worth the investment
since software will soon catch up to its amazing

00:08:39.349 --> 00:08:40.349
hardware.

00:08:40.349 --> 00:08:45.110
Also, if you’re a serious artist, the laminated
display, ProMotion tech, and Apple Pencil

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:49.760
2 make it the best option for drawing, and
you can get the Pro in the 12.9” size as

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:50.760
well.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:55.420
Now the iPad Air is the best all-around iPad
since it gets all of the amazing display tech,

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:59.740
the 10.5” size is great for most people
and the A12 processor is really powerful and

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:02.449
can run most of the apps and games that the
A12X can.

00:09:02.449 --> 00:09:06.010
It’ll also be fast enough for most photo
editing tasks as well.

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:10.339
The new Air is also the only non-Pro iPad
that comes with the smart connector, so if

00:09:10.339 --> 00:09:13.750
you’re planning on getting the smart keyboard
and you don’t want to spend the extra cash

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:18.100
on the Pro, the Air is a great all-around
long-term option for the price.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:22.780
Now the Mini is literally identical to the
Air in almost everything except that it doesn’t

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:27.449
get the smart connector and it packs the same
amount of pixels in a smaller display, so

00:09:27.449 --> 00:09:29.640
it’ll look sharper if you get up close to
it.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:33.779
It’s also $100 cheaper than the Air so you
can save a good amount if you’re fine with

00:09:33.779 --> 00:09:34.779
the small display.

00:09:34.779 --> 00:09:38.290
I’d also like to say that if you play a
lot of games, the Mini is the best choice

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:41.220
since it’s so comfortable to hold for longer
gaming sessions.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:45.959
It’s small, light, and portable, so it’ll
be a great option for kids as well.

00:09:45.959 --> 00:09:50.500
Now the budget iPad will also be a good option
for kids since the non-laminated display is

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:51.730
really cheap to replace.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:56.690
It’s the slowest out of the bunch, the display
and cameras are worse, but it’s also the

00:09:56.690 --> 00:10:00.260
cheapest, especially if you can find it on
sale for only $250 on Amazon.

00:10:00.260 --> 00:10:03.010
Check the link below to see if it’s still
on sale.

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:08.060
It’s a great budget option for everyone
who just needs a basic iPad to do iPad things,

00:10:08.060 --> 00:10:11.150
and it’ll be fine for most of the popular
games on the app store.

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:14.790
Well there you have it, if this comparison
didn’t help you make a decision, comment

00:10:14.790 --> 00:10:17.410
below with your specific situation and we’ll
help you out!

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:21.380
If you enjoyed this video, hit that subscribe
button for more videos like this one.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:30.839
This has been Vadim with Max Tech, and we’ll
see you in the next one!

